  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting World Hope&apos;s Annual Outing to Reduce Disability Stigma</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provide support to the Enable the Children&#x2019;s Beach Outing (24 Feb 2024) to contribute to our objectives on social inclusion and rights, including the UK&#x2019;s Disability Rights and Inclusion Strategy. Enable the Children is a programme under World Hope International, which was originally founded as an independent not-for-profit in 2007. The project provides home and clinic-based Physiotherapy and Occupational Therapy, and support services to approximately 1000 children living with disabilities in Freetown and different parts of Sierra Leone. In collaboration with the Ministry of Social Welfare, World Hope host an annual beach outing in Freetown. Supporting this event in a visual way would highlight UK support for disability inclusion and increase BHC visibility in this space. Assets will be re-used at future events by World Hope, thus creating ongoing visibility for the BHC/UK Development brand.</narrative>
  </description>
